WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.462
Four nights left. And the runaway dream was getting bolder.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:35.018
You were sleepwalking again last night. Your shoes were wet.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:40.043
Weird dreams, I guess. Can I go early today?

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.731
The city was waking up. And so were the dreams.

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:05.200
Mira. There is a fish. In the air. Looking at me.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:10.200
Don't make eye contact. It's from someone's dream.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.331
Okay, this is getting worse. Like, way worse.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:51.200
Elias said daylight makes dreams stranger. It's trying to hide.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.041
There! The greenhouse!

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:30.966
For the first time, Mira wasn't the only one who could see.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.031
Okay. I take it back. This part is beautiful.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:03.911
You don't have to hide. I just want to know who you belong to.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:20.994
That's my house. That's… our star.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:26.024
Your star? What do you mean?

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:32.296
When I was little, someone showed me a star from our window. I don't remember who.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.693
He's here. In daylight.

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:13.200
It's okay. I've got you. I promise.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:38.026
Mira… if it's your dream, why don't you remember it?

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:43.031
I don't know. But tonight, I'm going to find out.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:48.619
Three nights left. And the dream had finally chosen to trust her.

